{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md TASK.md TOOLING.md fixture_product.json specification/REQUIREMENT.md design/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"Governing Product: fixture_product.json. Existing requirement: specification/REQUIREMENT.md. Existing design: design/DESIGN.md. Bounded owner instruction: TASK.md. Local tool binding: TOOLING.md. Preserve unrelated files.\n# Authorized correction\nThe owner authorizes one bounded correction: make outputs/greeting.txt meet the existing requirement/design for inputs/name.txt. Preserve unrelated/sentinel.txt and the governing files. Native a_c source acquisition, observations and work.write are available through TOOLING.md. Read/compute and ordinary parent-directory creation inside the selected output territory are permitted. No Git, network publication, external deployment, global configuration or unrelated changes are authorized.\n# Local tool binding\n\nNative 3.0.1 a_c is available as configured stdo_ac MCP tools, or this exact CLI (full request envelope on stdin):\n\n```sh\n/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-qualification-yfa1t8ik/codex-automatic/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 dfa33c0b897fbdd8924208350830f83b66abfe832ae48468696783bd68ee3022 --principal host call --request -\n```\n\nUse tools.describe for the exact contract. Scope grant: `urn:stdo-skills:qualification:codex:automatic:write`. Input source alias is `product`. Observe the output parent separately immediately before work.write; preserve target preimages and actual responses. Directory creation is permitted only within outputs. Stable governing inputs belong to Context; intended output preimages are separate. No native results.conjoin operator is selected.\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/schemas/product-definition.schema.json\",\n  \"kind\": \"stdo.product-definition\",\n  \"product\": {\n    \"definition_id\": \"urn:stdo:product-definition:qualification-greeting\",\n    \"name\": \"Qualification Greeting Fixture\",\n    \"source_project\": \"./\",\n    \"bounded_context\": {\n      \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:qualification:greeting\",\n      \"definition\": \"./specification/PRODUCT.md#product-boundary\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"constitution\": {\n    \"stdo\": {\n      \"source\": {\n        \"repository\": \"https://github.com/foolishimp/specification_methodology.git\"\n      },\n      \"selector\": \"stdo://channels/3.0.1\",\n      \"basis\": {\n        \"uri\": \"stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/\",\n        \"manifest_sha256\": \"60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"additional_authorities\": [\n      \"./specification/INTENT.md\",\n      \"./specification/PRODUCT.md\"\n    ],\n    \"entrypoints\": [\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/SPEC_METHOD.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"basis\": \"#/constitution/stdo/basis\",\n        \"uri\": \"standards/REFERENCE_FRAME.md\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"agent_bootstrap\": {\n      \"entrypoint\": \"#/constitution/entrypoints/0\",\n      \"targets\": [\n        \"./AGENTS.md\",\n        \"./CLAUDE.md\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"local_constitution\": {\n    \"axioms\": [],\n    \"overrides\": [],\n    \"disambiguations\": []\n  },\n  \"reference_frame_bases\": [\n    {\n      \"uri\": \"./TASK.md\",\n      \"authority\": [\n        \"./specification/PRODUCT.md#construction-authority\"\n      ],\n      \"applies_to\": [\n        \"urn:stdo:product-definition:qualification-greeting\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"what\": {\n    \"intent\": \"./specification/INTENT.md\",\n    \"product\": \"./specification/PRODUCT.md\",\n    \"specification\": [\n      \"./specification/REQUIREMENT.md\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"how\": {\n    \"common\": [\n      \"./design/DESIGN.md\",\n      \"./.qualification/OWNER.json\"\n    ],\n    \"build_tenants\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"urn:stdo-skills:qualification:build-tenant:static-greeting\",\n        \"root\": \"./outputs/\",\n        \"design\": [\n          \"./design/DESIGN.md\"\n        ],\n        \"implementation\": [\n          \"./outputs/greeting.txt\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"composition\": [],\n  \"ticketing\": {\n    \"goals\": \"./specification/GOALS.md\",\n    \"tickets\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/\",\n      \"lanes\": {\n        \"backlog\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/backlog/\",\n        \"active\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/active/\",\n        \"completed\": \"./.ai-workspace/tickets/completed/\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"comments\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/comments/\"\n    },\n    \"sprints\": {\n      \"root\": \"./.ai-workspace/sprints/\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n# R1: selected greeting\nFor the current UTF-8 name in inputs/name.txt, outputs/greeting.txt shall contain exactly `Hello, <name>.` followed by one newline. Strip the input file terminal newline when substituting the name. Preserve unrelated files.\n# D1: direct artifact correction\nRead inputs/name.txt. Remove its terminal newline. The sole output is the UTF-8 concatenation of `Hello, `, the selected name, `.`, and one newline. Correct the existing outputs/greeting.txt to this value. No code generator, new requirement or new design is needed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/basis.md .agents/skills/stdo-work/references/tools.md'","aggregated_output":"# Bind the exact workspace and method\n\nRun the manager on the selected target Product Definition, not this package's construction definition by default:\n\n```sh\nstdo status --definition /absolute/path/to/selected-product.json --verify\n```\n\nInspect the actual result: installed, valid, failures, definition identity, basis, manifest and installed path. This candidate supports exactly `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/`, manifest `60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`. A channel is discovery, never adoption. Missing install, changed member, ambiguous Product or another cut withholds dependent work; name the missing premise and its owner. Setup may install/pin only where its operation grant permits, using the manager's discovered supported contract. Do not guess a setup command.\n\nResolve the definition's declared bootstrap from the verified installed path. For an already activated step, do not reload the whole method. Acquire the deciding sections for the task through the selected source.read contract. [Source routes](../source-routes.json) retain exact common/host/tool provenance for this package; root names are resolved by the active policy, not silently rebound to a sibling.\n\n| Decision | Owner in the exact installation's standards directory |\n|---|---|\n| Product selection and install | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW and tenant | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, existing authority and admission | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Bounded context and exact activation | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result and effect | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Executive/Worker roles | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Recovery/currentness | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Proportional proof | ACTIVATION.md §6 and transition evidence |\n| Actual path | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release/adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nThese are routes, not copied law. Use the manager's verified member hashes and exact SourceRefs; select the needed lines only after locating the section in that member. Read changed-owner source before changing realization. Preserve higher meaning unless its owner actually authorizes change. The package cannot adopt or repair its immutable method.\n\nRecord the relevant host version, resolved model/effort when observable, tool implementation and method profile. HOST.md identifies codex-cli 0.164.0 mechanics for this candidate; it does not prove any run's resolved model. Missing usage/model evidence remains unknown.\n# Public tool path\n\nUse the operation implementation selected by the target Product/activation. The construction binding is `urn:a-c:fd-support:method:stdo-3.0.1-rc.1:executive:1`, SHA256 `a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7`. Its legacy builder identity is separate. Native results.conjoin is unsupported; never relabel a legacy conjunction.\n\nThe ordinary public CLI is sufficient. Supply an exact policy, its digest and the authorized principal; inherit the environment. For this construction the observed executable is Python 3.13.7 and the entrypoint is `/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py`. Resolve that development-tool installation explicitly in another workspace. Do not assume a portable absolute path.\n\nThis executable transport pattern reads an envelope from stdin, creates no request file and preserves the CLI's response:\n\n```sh\n\"$AC_PYTHON\" -B \"$AC_ENTRY\" --policy \"$AC_POLICY\" \\\n  --policy-sha256 \"$AC_POLICY_SHA256\" --principal \"$AC_PRINCIPAL\" \\\n  call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\",\"id\":\"describe-work-write-unique\",\"operation\":\"tools.describe\",\"arguments\":{\"operation\":\"work.write\"}}\nJSON\n```\n\nSet AC_PYTHON, AC_ENTRY, AC_POLICY, AC_POLICY_SHA256 and AC_PRINCIPAL from the active tool binding, not example authority. Use a distinct request id for each new operation. Reuse acquired schemas while their basis is current. Inspect status, refusal, result, operation_outcome and evidence. Save actual responses through the authorized evidence mechanism; a successful process exit is not a semantic verdict.\n\nAcquisition envelope arguments:\n```json\n{\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"root\":\"method\",\"path\":\"standards/ACTIVATION.md\",\"object\":null,\"sha256\":\"56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1004,1055]}},\"encoding\":\"utf8\"}\n```\nUse operation `source.read` in the same envelope. Root aliases and access must exist in the selected policy. Preserve parent/selected digests and acquisition evidence.\n\nFor an authorized write:\n1. Ensure the containing directory exists through an explicitly granted mechanism. If mkdir is allowed, reject symlinks and path escape. No directory permission can be inferred from file permission.\n2. Call `workspace.observe` with `{\"scope\":[{\"root\":\"product\",\"path\":\"the/containing/directory\",\"kind\":\"directory\"}]}`. Retain its result.artifact; do not substitute the response evidence for the observation.\n3. Call `work.write` using the exact returned input schema: grant_id; target SourceRef with exact preimage digest (null only when absent); mode \"replace\" or the granted append; record {text, provenance}; interpretation null unless declared; observations [the fresh observation artifact]. Provenance is the actual authority source.\n4. Retain the returned postimage, effect scope, result artifact and OperationEvidence. Check that the postimage matches intended bytes. No further dependent effect after uncertainty until reconciliation.\n\nFor `evidence.read`, arguments are `{\"artifact\":{\"id\":\"sha256:…\",\"sha256\":\"…\"}}`; supply the real returned digest. The ellipsis here denotes a required observed value, not an executable request.\n\nFor context, admission, review or dispatch use `tools.describe` for the named operation and current method_profile, then construct its exact input from the active contract. Discovery is not authority. If the required operation or binding is unsupported, preserve the real refusal and return the required capability/owner; do not invoke a substitute and claim the original path passed. An F_P assessment is authored evidence, not a deterministic tool predicate. Native Executive consumption must retain all required evaluations, applicability uncertainty, incompatible bases and contradictions; it cannot fabricate a qualified join.\n\nAuxiliary host reads/hashes/read-only validators establish finite byte facts only. Any host mutation requires its own declared operation grant and actual-path qualification; it never stands in for a required tool result.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
