{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin/python3.13 -B /Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c/build_tenants/graphify/code/ac_support.py --policy /private/tmp/stdo-skills-qualification-yfa1t8ik/codex-automatic/control/worker-policy.json --policy-sha256 dfa33c0b897fbdd8924208350830f83b66abfe832ae48468696783bd68ee3022 --principal host call --request - <<'JSON'\n{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"a_c.fd-support.request/1\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"greeting-source-0-1\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"source.read\\\",\\\"arguments\\\":{\\\"source\\\":{\\\"engine\\\":\\\"workspace-regular-file\\\",\\\"object\\\":null,\\\"root\\\":\\\"method\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\\\",\\\"selector\\\":{\\\"lines\\\":[1,54]}},\\\"encoding\\\":\\\"utf8\\\"}}\nJSON\"","aggregated_output":"{\"evidence\":{\"id\":\"sha256:2accba1fe4f09b2037af5931136b580c898d495f688ca63f3e18088758b31479\",\"sha256\":\"2accba1fe4f09b2037af5931136b580c898d495f688ca63f3e18088758b31479\"},\"id\":\"greeting-source-0-1\",\"operation\":\"source.read\",\"operation_outcome\":{\"cause\":\"declared output available\",\"core_value\":\"satisfied\",\"evidence\":[],\"limits\":[\"output availability only; no semantic acceptance\"],\"predicate\":\"B(source.read)[request_sha256=da7d2ebc99c9ab4b64659f528a3000c47bbbda339660bb1bb74a3e01f9e3ec50]: declared output availability\",\"source_parent\":{\"clause\":\"results\",\"member\":\"FOUNDATIONS.md\",\"sha256\":\"92fe2f3c09a59b4e9a732463a41d4a45d7efd693648159621e03c75f7127eac5\"},\"value\":\"returned\"},\"refusal\":null,\"result\":{\"artifact\":null,\"value\":{\"acquisition\":{},\"content\":\"# Reference frame bootstrap\\n\\nTask: Enter this method for a task not yet specified: say what the method is, bind the exact basis and the one applicable product definition, say how a reference frame is activated for a step and what the step may and may not do before its contract is admitted, give the core result values, and acquire the deciding owner sections for the task.\\n\\nPurpose: The owning sections for the method's canonical statement; the product lineage objects; the product definition's required relations, recursive discovery and the one constitutional surface with its staleness binding; the authority kinds, the frame tuple and the activation packet; the step's intake and admission; context construction with the size measurement, acquisition, activation and evaluation; and the core result algebra.\\n\\nBinds:\\n\\n- This task binds the construction relation: A is the exact subject and basis the activation binds, Z is the task's required outcome with the acceptance conditions the task states, and the actor's claims keep preservation, progress and outcome satisfaction distinct; a judgment its evidence cannot decide is `indeterminate`, and work it cannot finish is reported as unresolved work, not as a judgment ([../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation](../ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation); member sha256=56109ffa2e8ec6f158e6dbd0b387fededa685abc100a288ea88525854a78441d; section sha256=6b6c2ce91c5a7e4be765af2f8009252fa8918719e1d885af6b5810ba4eb699da)\\n\\nA `Binds:` item names an obligation the activation of this frame binds, with\\na link to the owning section, the digest of its member and the digest of that\\nsection, or of the span of sections it names, where it names one; the item\\ncopies no section and owns no determination, and where no route of this frame\\ncarries the section the item is a paraphrase of it.\\n\\nEach excerpt below copies one owning section of a member of this method\\nbyte for byte, except a `rows=k/n` excerpt (see below) and except that\\neach relative link destination is rebased\\nto resolve from this directory to the same target. Fenced code, inline\\ncode and absolute and `stdo://` links are unchanged. The `Source:` line\\nbefore an excerpt names the member and the section's anchor, and gives\\nthe SHA-256 of the whole owning member. The section digest recorded in\\nFRAME_INPUTS.json is over the owner's bytes, not over this copy. The\\nowning section decides; this frame owns no determination. An excerpt\\nwhose `Source:` line says `rows=k/n` is a family table of which only\\nthe k rows that cite a section this frame carries are copied, with the\\ntable's preamble, header and every non-family table; the other rows\\nstay in the owning member and are not copied. The frame's\\nqualification, not this selection, decides whether the frame is\\nsufficient for its task.\\n\\nRoutes, in order:\\n\\n1. [SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement](../SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement)\\n2. [FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects](../FOUNDATIONS.md#product-lineage-objects)\\n3. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#2-required-definition-relations)\\n4. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#9-recursive-discovery-and-explicit-composition)\\n5. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#11-one-constitutional-surface-and-version-boundary)\\n6. [FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds](../FOUNDATIONS.md#authority-kinds)\\n7. [FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple](../FOUNDATIONS.md#the-frame-tuple)\\n8. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#11-the-activation-packet)\\n9. [ACTIVATION.md#intake](../ACTIVATION.md#intake)\\n10. [ACTIVATION.md#admission](../ACTIVATION.md#admission)\\n11. [ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope](../ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope)\\n12. [FOUNDATIONS.md#results](../FOUNDATIONS.md#results)\\n13. [PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method](../PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#foundation-to-law-binding-a-project-to-the-method)\\n14. [REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law](../REFERENCE_FRAME.md#foundation-to-law)\\n15. [SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding](../SPEC_METHOD.md#foundation-to-law-chain-outcome-and-build-tenant-binding)\\n\\nSize of this frame: 84475 bytes.\\n\\nSource: SPEC_METHOD.md#canonical-statement sha256=b2773dc0c9feb429b6b357bcfd60e7df46e54db8adcb04dc8d6dbfa023b73677\\n\\n\",\"coordinates\":{\"lines\":[1,54]},\"encoding\":\"utf8\",\"parent_sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\",\"selected_sha256\":\"20d01b72f62f884b556e7b2abd3ee12cab4733efa6d1257118da9c9189a21a61\",\"size_bytes\":4464,\"source\":{\"engine\":\"workspace-regular-file\",\"object\":null,\"path\":\"standards/frames/bootstrap.md\",\"root\":\"method\",\"selector\":{\"lines\":[1,54]},\"sha256\":\"cbf4a10e8d0b4ca2ab4a1f3ee28a85ffedc3298a0fba666949d9b091e82cc714\"}}},\"schema\":\"a_c.fd-support.response/1\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
